<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bitòn Coulibaly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1712–1755</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Mamari Kulibali, Biton Coulibaly, Mamari Coulibaly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bitòn Coulibaly, also called Mamari Kulibali, was the founder of the Bambara Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Ségou</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, ruling from about 1712 until his death in 1755. He turned a youth association, the ton, into a standing army bound to him and used captives as soldiers to conquer neighbouring lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. He made Ségou his capital and is remembered in Bambara epic tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/biton-coulibaly.jpg" alt="Bitòn Coulibaly" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KaTeznik · CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tombe_Biton_Coulibaly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
